<div id="S2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">In contrast, the next two options are possible and mutually exclusive:</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">vertices <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> are end-points of paths starting in a vertex <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>; see Fig. <a href="#S2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>(c);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the path from <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has a common edge with <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>; see Fig. <a href="#S2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Proof. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>(d).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">In both cases <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the subtree rooted at <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> since the path from <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has no common edges with <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. This subtree is inside <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}^{T_{0}}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}^{T_{0}}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> so its depth is at most <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell-2</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies that diameter of <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\ell-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\ell-4</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, any path starting in <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and containing <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>
should have length at most <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell-1</annotation></semantics></math>, by the minimality condition.
Since <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> contains <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and the path from <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> has at least 3 edges, the diameter of <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="S2.SS1.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\ell-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\ell-6</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> puts restrictions on extensions using ‘new’ edges only. Non-isomorphic <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-growths are possible in generation sequences even if <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>
has the diameter at least <math id="S2.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\ell-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\ell-6</annotation></semantics></math>; see an example in Fig. <a href="#S2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
