<figure id="S2.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2401.07484v2/1root-10-mps.svg" id="S2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="width:6.594em; height:6.081em;aspect-ratio:88/81;" width="88" height="81"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2401.07484v2/1root-11-mps.svg" id="S2.F5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="width:9.765em; height:6.619em;aspect-ratio:130/88;" width="130" height="88"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2401.07484v2/1root-12-mps.svg" id="S2.F5.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="width:9.765em; height:6.619em;aspect-ratio:130/88;" width="130" height="88"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2401.07484v2/1root-13-mps.svg" id="S2.F5.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="width:9.765em; height:7.856em;aspect-ratio:130/104;" width="130" height="104"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>A not mortal amoeba with one root with respect to <math id="S2.F5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-extensions. The next step uses the left lower <math id="S2.F5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> for extensions. Repetitions of the process continue forever</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">It is clear that the last tree in any generation sequence is confining. Thus, mortality implies the existence of a confining tree.
The converse is proven only for <math id="S2.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> and it remains open in general.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For extension parameter <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, an amoeba is mortal if and only if there exists a confining tree for it.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The ‘if part’ is obvious.
The ‘only if part’: take a confining tree and a copy of the amoeba. Start a generation sequence from this copy.
Note that <math id="S2.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>- and <math id="S2.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-growths of a copy of the amoeba in any tree are isomorphic.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, if an extension path from a root contains a new edge then the root should be a pendant vertex in the initial tree or should be adjacent to a pendant vertex since <math id="S2.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we add either a pendant edge or a path of length <math id="S2.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the tree that is the union of two different growths these edges or paths belong to the same orbit of automorphisms. Therefore, the different growths are isomorphic to each other.
This implies that at each step of extension new edges can be chosen from the confining tree. Therefore, the sequence is finite.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3</span></span><span id="Thmremark3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the general case it is open whether the immortality is the negation of mortality.
For the extension parameter <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> it is true due to <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
If an amoeba is not immortal then the last tree of its
finite generation sequence is a confining tree for the
amoeba.
Thus, all its generation sequences are finite.
So the amoeba is mortal.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">In the proof of the next theorem we will use the notion of full <math id="S2.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree of depth <math id="S2.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.
To this end we denote by <math id="S2.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{t,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{t,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> a rooted
tree in which every node at distance less than <math id="S2.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> from the root has <math id="S2.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> children, while
every node at distance <math id="S2.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is a leaf.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">An amoeba is
mortal w.r.t all trees
if and only if it is totally confined, regardless of its extension parameter.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> be the extension parameter.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">In one direction it is easy. Suppose an amoeba is mortal w.r.t all trees.
Take a tree <math id="S2.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="S2.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-growth sequence <math id="S2.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=T_{0},\dots,T_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=T_{0},\dots,T_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> starting in <math id="S2.SS1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. It is finite and the last tree <math id="S2.SS1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in the sequence confines the amoeba and contains <math id="S2.SS1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the other direction, take a tree <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a totally confined amoeba <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\max_{v\in V(H)}\big(d(v)+m(v)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\max_{v\in V(H)}\big(d(v)+m(v)\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=\mathop{\mathrm{diam}}(T_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">diam</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=\mathop{\mathrm{diam}}(T_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose a confining tree <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> that contains a full <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-ary tree <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\delta,3\ell+2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\delta,3\ell+2d}</annotation></semantics></math> of sufficiently large depth, say, <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\ell+2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\ell+2d</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choose a copy of <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> containing the center of <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\delta,3\ell+2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\delta,3\ell+2d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Start <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-growth sequence <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0},T_{1},\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0},T_{1},\dots</annotation></semantics></math> from this particular copy.
If <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\mathrm{diam}}(T_{i})\leq 2\ell-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">diam</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathrm{diam}}(T_{i})\leq 2\ell-6</annotation></semantics></math> then any copy of <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> in it is at distance at most <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\ell-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\ell-6</annotation></semantics></math> from the center of <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\delta,3\ell+2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\delta,3\ell+2d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, any growth of <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be embedded to <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
If an <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-growth of <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> uses edges of <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the corresponding copy of <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is at distance at most <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2d</annotation></semantics></math> from the center of <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\delta,3\ell+2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\delta,3\ell+2d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, again, the growth can be embedded to <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
If an <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-growth of <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> does not use edges of <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\mathrm{diam}}(T_{i})&gt;2\ell-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">diam</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathrm{diam}}(T_{i})&gt;2\ell-6</annotation></semantics></math>, then <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> implies that all such growths are isomorphic.
So we apply the same arguments as in the proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and conclude that <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> can be embedded in <math id="S2.SS1.p14.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the sequence is finite.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Orbit lemma</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix an amoeba <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a vertex <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(H)</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the <em id="S2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">orbit</em> of <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\mathrm{Orb}}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">Orb</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathrm{Orb}}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, as the set of vertices <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in V(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in V(H)</annotation></semantics></math> such that there exists an automorphism of <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> mapping <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <em id="S2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">completion</em> <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math> of amoeba <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]=(H,m^{\prime}),\qquad m^{\prime}(v)=\max_{w\in\mathop{\mathrm{Orb}}(v)}m(w)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">∈</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">Orb</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]=(H,m^{\prime}),\qquad m^{\prime}(v)=\max_{w\in\mathop{\mathrm{Orb}}(v)}m(w).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We call a pair of amoebas <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}=(H,m^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}=(H,m^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="S2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">equivalent</em> (to each other) if <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]=[A^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]=[A^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using this notation one can easily obtain the following claim.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> be the extension parameter and <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math> be an amoeba.
If <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is mortal if and only if its completion is.
For other values of <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, an amoeba is
mortal w.r.t all trees
if and only if its completion is.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start from the case <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math> is mortal, that is, it admits a confining tree <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. It remains to observe that <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> confines also <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is mortal by <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now suppose that <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is mortal. <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> implies that there exists a confining tree <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H,m^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H,m^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> be a copy of <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(H)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be a vertex in <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\mathrm{Orb}}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">Orb</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\mathrm{Orb}}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(v^{*})=m^{\prime}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(v^{*})=m^{\prime}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the choice of <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an automorphism of <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> mapping <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding copy of the amoeba <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math> has an <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-extension inside <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. It means that <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> can be extended by <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> paths of length <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> such that the paths have the only common vertex <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and each of these paths has the only common vertex <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By using such paths at each vertex of <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, one can construct an <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-extension of any copy of <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. It means that <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> confines <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>, similar arguments show that an amoeba is
not mortal w.r.t some tree
if and only if its completion is. The only difference is in applying <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> instead of <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Case of <math id="S3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-extensions</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Understanding the mortality of general amoebas seems to be very difficult.
In this section we focus on the mortality conditions for amoebas which grow in the simplest of ways -- by attaching pendant edges.<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          In our notation such amoeba growth corresponds to the case of <math id="footnote3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-extensions.</span></span></span>
In <a href="#Thmremark3" title="Remark 3. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Remark</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> we explained that for this case, immortality is just the negation of mortality.
The results of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> easily imply that
any immortal amoeba is subcubic whenever the number of roots is equal to <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.
The following subsection generalizes those results to the case of arbitrary number of roots.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Degree conditions</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the rest of this subsection fix an immortal amoeba <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d(v),m(v))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d(v),m(v))</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in H</annotation></semantics></math>, be the sequence of vertex degrees and multiplicities of the roots in <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. We also define
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{m}=\max_{v\in V(H)}(d(v)+m(v))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{m}=\max_{v\in V(H)}(d(v)+m(v))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fix an infinite <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-generation sequence <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0},G_{1},\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0},G_{1},\dots</annotation></semantics></math>.
The next claim immediately follows from the definition of the <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-extension.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If a vertex <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a root of a copy of the amoeba to be extended and
<math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G_{i+1}}(v)&gt;d_{G_{i}}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G_{i+1}}(v)&gt;d_{G_{i}}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G_{i}}(v)&lt;d_{H}(v)+m(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G_{i}}(v)&lt;d_{H}(v)+m(v)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G_{i}}(v)\geq d_{H}(v)+m(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G_{i}}(v)\geq d_{H}(v)+m(v)</annotation></semantics></math> then an extension uses existing edges incident to <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> due to the minimality condition.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 7</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G_{i}}(v)\leq\widetilde{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G_{i}}(v)\leq\widetilde{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(G_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(G_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This corollary provides a uniform upper bound on vertex degrees in all graphs <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. From this we derive the following.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 8</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and sufficiently large <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, vertices of a copy extending at step <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> do not intersect <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">If a vertex <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(G_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(G_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to a copy of the amoeba extending at some step, then a new pendant edge is added at distance at most <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V(H)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V(H)|</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since all degrees of vertices in all graphs in the generation sequence are bounded by <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{m}</annotation></semantics></math> due to <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Corollary 7. ‣ 3.1 Degree conditions ‣ 3 Case of 1-extensions ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, it can repeat
finitely many times.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">These facts put restrictions on degrees of vertices in <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that we add pendant edges. So, initially a degree of a new vertex <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is 1.
Then it can be increased by extension of a copy having a root at <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, <math id="S3.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\min_{v:m(v)&gt;0}d(v)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{v:m(v)&gt;0}d(v)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To catch the process of degree increasing, we introduce an auxiliary
directed graph <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The vertices of <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> are positive integers up to <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A pair <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is an edge in <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=d(v)+m(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=d(v)+m(v)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(v)+m(v)&gt;x\geq d(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(v)+m(v)&gt;x\geq d(v)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S3.SS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(H)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be the maximal integer reachable from 1 in <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the definition of <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, the inequality <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\leq\widetilde{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\leq\widetilde{m}</annotation></semantics></math> holds.
For an immortal amoeba,
let <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be such that
<math id="S3.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{m}=d(v^{*})+m(v^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{m}=d(v^{*})+m(v^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is reachable because <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(v^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(v^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> appears in a new vertex (i.e. a vertex from <math id="S3.SS1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G_{i})\setminus V(G_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G_{i})\setminus V(G_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>) and all copies containing this vertex at some moment have enough space for the extension. This implies the following theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 9</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let
<math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math> be an immortal amoeba
with its auxiliary digraph <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then
<math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{A}=\widetilde{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{A}=\widetilde{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{H}(v)\leq\widetilde{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{H}(v)\leq\widetilde{m}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V(H)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 10</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any amoeba <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> roots, we have <math id="Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{m}\leq 1+k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{m}\leq 1+k</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2},\dots,x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2},\dots,x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be a directed path in <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition of <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[1,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[1,t]</annotation></semantics></math> there exists <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}\in V(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}\in V(H)</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S3.SS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=d(v_{i})+m(v_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=d(v_{i})+m(v_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i-1}\geq d(v_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i-1}\geq d(v_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex3X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{1}\leq 1;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{1}\leq 1;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex3Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{2}=d(v_{2})+m(v_{2})\leq 1+m(v_{2});" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{2}=d(v_{2})+m(v_{2})\leq 1+m(v_{2});</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex3Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex3Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t}\leq 1+\sum_{j=2}^{t}m(v_{j})\leq 1+\sum_{v\in V(H)}m(v)=1+k." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t}\leq 1+\sum_{j=2}^{t}m(v_{j})\leq 1+\sum_{v\in V(H)}m(v)=1+k.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">The last inequality follows from the fact that each <math id="S3.SS1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> can appear along the path only once.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 11</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math> be an immortal amoeba such that <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(H)\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(H)\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 12</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math> be an amoeba.
If <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(H)&gt;k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(H)&gt;k+1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is mortal.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The following generalization of the above corollary remains open.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmconjecture1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_conjecture">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmconjecture1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conjecture 1</span></span><span id="Thmconjecture1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmconjecture1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmconjecture1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any value of the extension parameter <math id="Thmconjecture1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>,
and amoeba <math id="Thmconjecture1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmconjecture1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of roots in <math id="Thmconjecture1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="Thmconjecture1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(H)&gt;k+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(H)&gt;k+2</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="Thmconjecture1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is totally confined.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Mortality criteria for caterpillars</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection a <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-extension of a given amoeba will be referred to simply as an <em id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">extension</em>.
Furthermore, throughout this section we assume that the multiplicity function <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> takes values <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> only.
A <em id="S3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">caterpillar</em> <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(d_{1},d_{2},\dots,d_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(d_{1},d_{2},\dots,d_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> is a tree constructed as follows.
We start with a <em id="S3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">central path</em> <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\ell}=(p_{1},\dots,p_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\ell}=(p_{1},\dots,p_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>, and afterwards, for each <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,\ell\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,\ell\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we add <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> pendant vertices to <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In addition, we require <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1}=d_{\ell}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1}=d_{\ell}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
A caterpillar is said to be symmetric if <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}=d_{\ell-i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}=d_{\ell-i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
The family of amoebas <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is a caterpillar and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> respects the above-mentioned properties is denoted by <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this section we characterize mortality of amoebas from <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_observation">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Observation 13</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be a caterpillar with central path <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\subseteq V(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\subseteq V(H)</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(H,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(H,m)</annotation></semantics></math> be an amoeba such that <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\supp(m)\subseteq P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\supp(m)\subseteq P</annotation></semantics></math>.
An extension of <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>
gives rise to a caterpillar.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2401.07484v2/cat-10-mps.svg" id="S3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="width:12.617em; height:6.484em;aspect-ratio:168/86;" width="168" height="86"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2401.07484v2/cat-11-mps.svg" id="S3.F6.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="width:15.518em; height:6.484em;aspect-ratio:206/86;" width="206" height="86"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>A caterpillar <math id="S3.F6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C(0,2,2,3,0),m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C(0,2,2,3,0),m)</annotation></semantics></math> and its extension <math id="S3.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(0,0,2,3,4,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(0,0,2,3,4,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is enough to observe that the central path of the obtained graph corresponds to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, possibly with an additional vertex on either endpoint of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> (also see <a href="#S3.F6" title="In 3.2 Mortality criteria for caterpillars ‣ 3 Case of 1-extensions ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now give a necessary and sufficient condition for an amoeba from <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> to be shiftable ‘to the right’.
We start with some definitions.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(of slow integer sequences)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=(d_{1},d_{2},\dots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=(d_{1},d_{2},\dots)</annotation></semantics></math> be an integer sequence.
We say that <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">slowly decreasing</em>, if <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}-d_{i-1}\geq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}-d_{i-1}\geq-1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i},d_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i},d_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">slowly increasing</em>, if <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}-d_{i-1}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}-d_{i-1}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i},d_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i},d_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">slow</em> if it is either slowly increasing or slowly decreasing.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(of slow amoebas)<span id="Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For an integer sequence <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>
let <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{1},\dots,p_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{1},\dots,p_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> be the central path of <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(S)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C(S),m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C(S),m)</annotation></semantics></math> be an amoeba from <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The amoeba <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C(S),m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C(S),m)</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be</p>
<ul id="S3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">slowly decreasing</em> if <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is slowly decreasing
and the roots are placed at <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}-d_{i-1}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}-d_{i-1}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and also in <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">slowly increasing</em> if <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is slowly decreasing and the roots are placed at <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}-d_{i-1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}-d_{i-1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and also in <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">slow</em> if it is either slowly increasing or slowly decreasing.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 14</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">An amoeba <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is mortal if and only if <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math> is not slow.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=(d_{1},d_{2},\dots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=(d_{1},d_{2},\dots)</annotation></semantics></math> be the degree sequence of the central path of <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math>.
To prove the ‘if direction’ assume w.l.o.g. that <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math> is slowly decreasing.
We define a sequence of graphs <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=(G_{1},G_{2},\dots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=(G_{1},G_{2},\dots)</annotation></semantics></math>,
starting with <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}=C(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}=C(S)</annotation></semantics></math>.
(Informally speaking, <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of ‘right shifts’ of <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math>.)
Every member of this sequence is a caterpillar graph, hence, the vertex notation (vertices <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\dots</annotation></semantics></math>) is well defined.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Within <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> define a set of vertices <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}\subseteq V(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}\subseteq V(G)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}=\{p_{i},\dots,p_{i+|S|}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}=\{p_{i},\dots,p_{i+|S|}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a copy <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(S)</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained from <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by extending <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Due to <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 2.1 Initial observations ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> of the ‘if direction’ of the statement, it is enough to prove that <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> is infinite.
Assume for contradiction that <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> has (a finite) length <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.
By definition <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}=C(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}=C(S)</annotation></semantics></math>
contains <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence, <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> does not admit a copy of <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(S)</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, either</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">there is an <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G_{k}}(p_{k+i})&lt;d_{i}+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G_{k}}(p_{k+i})&lt;d_{i}+2</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;|S|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;|S|</annotation></semantics></math>, or</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G_{k}}(p_{k+i})&lt;d_{i}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G_{k}}(p_{k+i})&lt;d_{i}+1</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=|S|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=|S|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that (<a href="#S3.I3.i2" title="Item ii ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2 Mortality criteria for caterpillars ‣ 3 Case of 1-extensions ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">ii</span></a>) implies <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G_{k}}(p_{k+|S|})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G_{k}}(p_{k+|S|})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which is impossible.
Let us fix an <math id="S3.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying (<a href="#S3.I3.i1" title="Item i ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2 Mortality criteria for caterpillars ‣ 3 Case of 1-extensions ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">i</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">By construction, there exists a copy <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(S)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> whose extension gives rise to <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. By (<a href="#S3.I3.i1" title="Item i ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2 Mortality criteria for caterpillars ‣ 3 Case of 1-extensions ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">i</span></a>) we have <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}-d_{i-1}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}-d_{i-1}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>; furthermore, <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}-d_{i-1}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}-d_{i-1}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is slowly decreasing.
However, due to the extension of <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]=(H,m^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]=(H,m^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we are guaranteed that
<math id="S3.SS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}(p_{k+i})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}(p_{k+i})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
and hence
<math id="S3.SS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G_{k}}(p_{k+i})-2\geq d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G_{k}}(p_{k+i})-2\geq d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a contradiction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove the ‘only if direction’ of the claim assume that <math id="S3.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]=(H,m^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]=(H,m^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is neither slowly increasing nor slowly decreasing.
This can be due to one of the following reasons. There exist:</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}-d_{i-1}&lt;-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}-d_{i-1}&lt;-1</annotation></semantics></math>, while
<math id="S3.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}-d_{j-1}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}-d_{j-1}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}-d_{i-1}&lt;-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}-d_{i-1}&lt;-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}-d_{j-1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}-d_{j-1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="S3.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is not a root;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}-d_{i-1}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}-d_{i-1}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}-d_{j-1}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}-d_{j-1}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, while
<math id="S3.I4.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is not a root;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I4.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S3.I4.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}-d_{i-1}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}-d_{i-1}=-1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.I4.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}-d_{j-1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}-d_{j-1}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, while neither <math id="S3.I4.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> nor <math id="S3.I4.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j-1}</annotation></semantics></math> are roots.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the central path <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{1},\dots,p_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{1},\dots,p_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> in an arbitrary copy of <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In all four above cases
the following claim holds:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 15</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all copies of <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sets <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{2},\dots,p_{\ell-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{2},\dots,p_{\ell-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> coincide.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, any path of length <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell-1</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contains a pendant vertex either from <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(G_{2})\setminus V(G_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(G_{2})\setminus V(G_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> or from <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and in the latter case it is adjacent to either <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S3.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\ell-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\ell-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In fact, the former case of this alternative is possible only if the amoeba is slow. Otherwise, one of the cases listed above holds.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote by <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p^{\prime}_{1},\dots,p^{\prime}_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p^{\prime}_{1},\dots,p^{\prime}_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> the vertices of <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> which correspond to <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{1},\dots,p_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{1},\dots,p_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <a href="#Thmtheorem15" title="Lemma 15. ‣ Proof. ‣ 3.2 Mortality criteria for caterpillars ‣ 3 Case of 1-extensions ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>,
for <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;i\leq\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;i\leq\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that either</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}_{i}=p_{i-1},\text{ or}\quad p^{\prime}_{i}=p_{i},\text{ or}\quad p^{\prime}_{i}=p_{\ell-i+1},\text{ or}\quad p^{\prime}_{i}=p_{\ell-i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext> or</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext> or</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext> or</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}_{i}=p_{i-1},\text{ or}\quad p^{\prime}_{i}=p_{i},\text{ or}\quad p^{\prime}_{i}=p_{\ell-i+1},\text{ or}\quad p^{\prime}_{i}=p_{\ell-i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">In all four cases, we obtain a contradiction with the vertex degrees’ conditions in <math id="S3.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">To finish the proof, take a copy <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that its central path contains a pendant vertex <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> adjacent to <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\ell-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\ell-1}</annotation></semantics></math>; the case when it is adjacent to <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is proved similarly.
To have enough room for <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to grow, we add one pendant edge to <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> only.
Notice that no new copies of <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math> appear, thus <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A]</annotation></semantics></math> is mortal, and due to <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ 2.2 Orbit lemma ‣ 2 Amoebas ‣ Growing Trees and Amoebas’ Replications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, so is <math id="S3.SS2.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
